\ Benchmark: the quadratic naive string builder (pairwise #append).
\
\ Counts are kept small: pairwise #append re-copies the growing accumulator on
\ every fragment, and each intermediate string is retained for the eval, so the
\ bytes copied and held grow as O(n^2). The interpreter's per-fragment loop cost
\ dominates wall time at these counts, so the quadratic shows up mainly in
\ retained bytes; run under `run --benchmark=verbose` to see total bytes grow
\ quadratically as the count doubles.

use "./string_assembly_common.1z" ;

"--- naive pairwise #append (quadratic) ---" print-line

[
  "naive tiny 1k"   [ tiny-frag 1000 build-naive drop ] benchmark-run
  "naive tiny 2k"   [ tiny-frag 2000 build-naive drop ] benchmark-run
  "naive tiny 4k"   [ tiny-frag 4000 build-naive drop ] benchmark-run
  "naive tiny 8k"   [ tiny-frag 8000 build-naive drop ] benchmark-run
] run-benchmarks
